  "prefLabel": "Dec 205.01 Declaratory Rulings",
  "priorExpiration": "2001-03-17",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Dec 205.01 Declaratory Rulings.\n\n(a) A person seeking a declaratory ruling on any matter within the jurisdiction of the committee shall request such ruling by filing a written petition.\n\n(b) Such a petition shall be verified under oath or affirmation by an authorized representative of the petitioner with knowledge of the relevant facts.\n\n(c) The committee shall dismiss a petition for declaratory ruling that:\n\n(1) Fails to set forth factual allegations that are definite and concrete;\n\n(2) Involves a hypothetical situation or otherwise seeks advice as to how the committee would decide a future case; or\n\n(3) Does not implicate the legal rights or responsibilities of the petitioner.\n\n(d) Except for a petition dismissed pursuant to subsection (c), the committee shall conduct an adjudicative proceeding on a petition for declaratory ruling in accordance with Dec 203.\n\nSource. #4235, eff 2-20-87, EXPIRED: 2-20-93\n\nNew. #5700, INTERIM, eff 9-17-93, EXPIRED: 1-15-94\n\nNew. #5824, eff 8-30-94, EXPIRED: 8-30-00\n\nNew. #7366, INTERIM, eff 9-18-00, EXPIRED: 3-17-01\n\nNew. #9144-A eff 4-25-08",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/dec100-200.html"
